            <ArticleTitle>Continuous intravenous infusion of fentanyl: case reports of use in patients with advanced cancer and intractable pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>215-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The use of continuous intravenous infusion of opioids may be efficacious in managing pain related to advanced cancer. Short-acting opioids, such as morphine and hydromorphone, are commonly used. We describe the use of a fentanyl infusion in four cases. This experience suggests that fentanyl may be considered an alternative drug for infusion in the treatment of refractory cancer pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
